# Our changelog:

2026-10-29 Elena Sanchez  <el8432sa-s@student.lu.se>

	Added support for running the project as a SLURM batch job on COSMOS.

	* Updated scripts/runproject.sh to run the Apptainer container directly, avoiding the XAUTHORITY mount failure in batch jobs.
	* ChatGPT was used to help solve the XAUTHORITY mount failure.
	* Updated slurm/project.sbatch with a reusable batch configuration requesting 5 minutes and 1 GiB of memory.
	* Tested batch execution on COSMOS; the job completed successfully and generated all seven sunshine and temperature PDF plots.

2026-10-28 Elena Sanchez  <el8432sa-s@student.lu.se>

	Improved temperature analysis code and visualizations.

	* Improved comments in the temperature analysis code for clarity.
	* Refined temperature plotting code and yearly temperature visualizations.
	* Removed standardDeviations from TemperatureProfile because it is not used in the current plots.
  
2026-10-28 Gabriel Corrigan Förnvik <ga5705co-s@student.lu.se>

	Added a function to analyse the extracted data and return the means and std deviations - then used in a plotting function which was also implemented.

	* Modified precipitation.h to add new DailyStats type and declare the functions.
	* Implemented the functions in precipitation.cxx using standard functionality for the statistical calculation and ROOT TH1D for generating the plots. 
	* Modified main.cxx to test the new functionality.

2026-10-27 Elena Sanchez  <el8432sa-s@student.lu.se>

	Added yearly temperature plots and improved temperature comparison figures.

	* Added plots showing daily mean temperatures for individual years in Lund and Umeå, with the 2011–2025 average.
	* Added labels identifying individual years and the overall average in the yearly plots.
	* Improved plot titles and line widths for readability.
	* Updated the seasonal comparison plot to show the mean temperature curves without error bars.
	* Updated main.cxx and temperature_plot.h to generate the new yearly plots.

2026-10-27 Gabriel Corrigan Förnvik <ga5705co-s@student.lu.se>

	Added code to extract the precipitation data, the external CSV library, and the results folder

	* Added precipitation.h and precipitation.cxx with measurement class containing data for each observation.
	* Made a function to extract the data of the CSV:s, returning a vector of measurement objects. The function makes use of the CSV library and dayOfYear in `parse_csv.h` to convert month-day to a number 1-365, excluding Feb 29th in leap years.
	* Added results/ folder structure in order for main to run
	* Added external library csv/csv.h in include/
	* Modified main.cxx and makefile to implement data extraction and test it

2026-10-27 Elena Sanchez  <el8432sa-s@student.lu.se>

	Added temperature data processing and seasonal temperature analysis for Lund and Umeå.

	* Added a temperature CSV parser to handle the temperature data header and four-column format, and updated main.cxx to use it for the temperature datasets.
	* Added daily mean temperature calculation for the 2011–2025 analysis period, requiring at least two valid observations per day.
	* Added tracking of temperature data quality flags for daily observations.
	* Added seasonal mean temperature calculation by day of year, using a common 365-day calendar, excluding February 29 and shifting subsequent leap-year dates by one day.
	* Added calculation of the standard deviation of daily mean temperatures for each day of the year.
	* Added ROOT plotting of seasonal mean temperatures for Lund and Umeå with standard-deviation error bars.
	* Updated the Makefile and main.cxx to include and run the temperature analysis and plotting.

2026-10-26 Georges Nguyen <ge5787ng-s@student.lu.se>
	Data analysis for mean annual temperature
	* Formed preliminary histogram for single plots and comparison plots. 

2026-10-26 Manuel Lorente Rodriguez <ma8310lo-s@student.lu.se>
	Reorganized and simplified solar irradiance calculations and added three plotting functions.

	* Modified include/sunshine.h and src/sunshine.cxx to simplify the daily and yearly average calculations by reusing the sunshineByYearAndDay function.
	* Created include/sunshine_plot.h and src/sunshine_plot.cxx to separate data processing from ROOT visualization.
	* Implemented three plotting functions:
		* Daily solar irradiation comparison between Lund and Umeå, showing their average.
		* Daily solar irradiation histogram showing the average with individual years displayed as transparent curves in the background.
		* Annual mean solar irradiance comparison between Lund and Umeå, including linear regression fits.

2026-10-25 Manuel Lorente Rodriguez <ma8310lo-s@student.lu.se>
